    summary: "日本電信業者KDDI於6月23日發布公告，揭露其提供給網際網路服務商（ISP）的電子郵件系統遭到入侵。此次事件影響了包括BIGLOBE、Nifty、JCOM等6家ISP業者，可能導致多達1,422萬筆用戶的電子郵件帳號與密碼外洩。外洩的資料可能包含電子郵件地址與密碼，甚至涵蓋已停用或長期未使用的帳號。由於這些ISP共用KDDI的郵件系統平臺，單一漏洞事件便同時波及多家用戶。KDDI調查後確認，攻擊者是利用郵件系統所使用的第三方軟體漏洞進入系統。KDDI已於發現未授權存取後立即修補系統並採取防護措施，並已向相關ISP及日本主管機關通報。公司呼籲所有受影響的用戶，務必立即變更郵件密碼，以降低帳號被盜用的風險。",
    tags: ["KDDI", "ISP", "電子郵件系統", "第三方軟體漏洞", "資料外洩", "帳號密碼"],
    title_en: "KDDI Email System Breached: Accounts and Passwords of Up to 6 ISPs Affected Due to Third-Party Software Vulnerability",
    summary_en: "Japanese telecommunications carrier KDDI announced on June 23rd that its email system, provided to Internet Service Providers (ISPs), was compromised. The incident affected six ISPs, including BIGLOBE, Nifty, and JCOM, potentially leading to the leakage of up to 14.22 million user email accounts and passwords. The leaked data may include email addresses and passwords, and may even cover deactivated or long-unused accounts. Because these ISPs share KDDI's email system platform, a single vulnerability incident simultaneously impacted multiple users. KDDI investigated and confirmed that attackers gained access by exploiting a vulnerability in a third-party software used by the email system. KDDI immediately patched the system and implemented protective measures after discovering the unauthorized access, and has notified the relevant ISPs and Japanese regulatory authorities. The company urges all affected users to immediately change their email passwords to mitigate the risk of account theft.",
    tags_en: ["KDDI", "ISP", "Email System", "Third-Party Software Vulnerability", "Data Leakage", "Account Password"],
