    summary_en: "The UK's National Crime Agency (NCA) announced that two members of the cybercrime group Scattered Spider, Thalha Jubair and Owen Flowers, admitted to having breached the London Transport Authority's (TfL) computer network between August 31 and September 3, 2024. This attack resulted in losses and recovery costs for TfL reaching £29 million, affecting thousands of customers and forcing 28,000 employees to reset their passwords. Furthermore, the Oyster refund system data was illegally accessed. The NCA also discovered that the perpetrators had previously breached the networks of the US-based SSM Health Care Corporation and Sutter Health. Scattered Spider is a profit-driven criminal organization that frequently uses social engineering tactics, impersonating internal staff to trick victims into resetting passwords or providing multi-factor authentication information, subsequently leading to data theft or the deployment of ransomware. This incident highlights the extremely high risk faced by large public infrastructure when confronted with human social engineering attacks.",
