    title: "Linux 核心漏洞：Thunderbolt 驅動程式存在緩衝區溢出，可能導致遠端程式碼執行",
    summary: "本漏洞（CVE-2026-53148）存在於 Linux 核心的 Thunderbolt 驅動程式（`drivers/thunderbolt/xdomain.c`）。攻擊者可透過惡意對等點（peer）設定響應標頭的長度，使其超過預先分配的資料緩衝區，導致 `memcpy` 函式寫入超出分配範圍的記憶體，造成緩衝區溢出（Buffer Overflow）。此漏洞的攻擊向量為本地（L），複雜度為高（H），但權限要求為低（L），且無需使用者互動（UI:N）。修補建議是更新 Linux 核心到修復了此問題的最新版本。Red Hat 等主要發行版已提供修補資訊，建議系統管理員應立即升級核心版本以修復此安全風險。",
    tags: ["Linux 核心", "Thunderbolt", "CVE-2026-53148", "緩衝區溢出", "Red Hat", "Linux 驅動程式"],
    title_en: "Linux Kernel Vulnerability: Thunderbolt Driver Contains Buffer Overflow, Potentially Leading to Remote Code Execution",
    summary_en: "This vulnerability (CVE-2026-53148) resides in the Thunderbolt driver within the Linux kernel (`drivers/thunderbolt/xdomain.c`). An attacker can exploit this by setting the response header length of a malicious peer to exceed the pre-allocated data buffer, causing the `memcpy` function to write beyond the allocated memory and resulting in a Buffer Overflow. The attack vector for this vulnerability is local (L), the complexity is high (H), but the required privileges are low (L), and no user interaction is needed (UI:N). The recommended mitigation is to update the Linux kernel to the latest version that addresses this issue. Major distributions like Red Hat have provided patch information, and system administrators are advised to immediately upgrade the kernel version to fix this security risk.",
