    id: "20260625-033",
    trackers: ["os", "security"],
    category: "Linux",
    title: "Linux 核心漏洞：Thunderbolt 驅動程式的根目錄內容解析存在越界讀取風險",
    summary: "本漏洞涉及 Linux 核心的 Thunderbolt 驅動程式（位於 drivers/thunderbolt/property.c）。問題點在於 `__tb_property_parse_dir()` 函式在處理根目錄（root directory）的內容時，缺乏對內容偏移量（content_offset）和內容長度（content_len）的邊界檢查。當根目錄的長度達到或超過區塊長度減去 2 時，程式會執行超出分配屬性區塊的讀取操作，造成越界讀取（Out-of-bounds read）。此漏洞的修復建議是在計算 `content_offset` 和 `content_len` 之後，增加邊界檢查機制，以拒絕任何內容延伸超出區塊的目錄。受影響的 Linux 核心版本範圍較廣，建議系統管理員應立即更新至修補版本，以確保系統的安全性。",
    tags: ["Linux 核心", "Thunderbolt", "越界讀取", "CVE-2026-53149", "Linux Kernel"],
    title_en: "Linux Kernel Vulnerability: Out-of-bounds Read Risk in Thunderbolt Driver's Root Directory Content Parsing",
    summary_en: "This vulnerability affects the Thunderbolt driver within the Linux kernel (located at drivers/thunderbolt/property.c). The issue lies in the `__tb_property_parse_dir()` function, which fails to perform boundary checks on the content offset and content length when processing the root directory's content. When the root directory's length reaches or exceeds the block length minus 2, the program executes a read operation beyond the allocated property block, causing an Out-of-bounds read. The suggested fix for this vulnerability is to implement boundary checks after calculating `content_offset` and `content_len`, thereby rejecting any directory content that extends beyond the block. Since the affected Linux kernel versions are broad, system administrators are advised to immediately update to the patched version to ensure system security.",
    tags_en: ["Linux Kernel", "Thunderbolt", "Out-of-bounds read", "CVE-2026-53149", "Linux Kernel"],
    sources: [
      { name: "NVD CVE API", url: "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-53149", lang: "EN" }
    ]
