    category: "Linux",
    title: "Linux 核心漏洞：Thunderbolt 驅動程式允許零長度屬性條目導致緩衝區溢出",
    summary: "本漏洞存在於 Linux 核心的 Thunderbolt 驅動程式（位於 drivers/thunderbolt/property.c）。當驗證器 `tb_property_entry_valid()` 接受到零長度的屬性條目時，雖然該條目通過了驗證，但在後續的空終止字元邏輯處理中，會導致指標計算錯誤，進而造成緩衝區溢出（underflow）。具體來說，當屬性長度為 0 時，程式會嘗試寫入相對於分配位址 -1 的偏移量。此漏洞的實務影響是允許攻擊者利用零長度屬性條目來執行記憶體寫入操作，可能導致系統崩潰或遠端代碼執行。修補建議是應在驗證器早期階段就拒絕零長度的屬性條目，因為在 XDomain 屬性協定中，零長度條目本身沒有有效的表示意義。建議升級到已修補的 Linux 核心版本。",
    tags: ["Linux 核心", "Thunderbolt", "緩衝區溢出", "CVE-2026-53150", "drivers/thunderbolt/property.c"],
    title_en: "Linux Kernel Vulnerability: Thunderbolt Driver Allows Zero-Length Attribute Entry Leading to Buffer Overflow",
    summary_en: "This vulnerability exists in the Linux kernel's Thunderbolt driver (located in drivers/thunderbolt/property.c). When the validator `tb_property_entry_valid()` receives a zero-length attribute entry, although the entry passes validation, subsequent null-terminator logic processing leads to an incorrect pointer calculation, causing a buffer underflow. Specifically, when the attribute length is 0, the program attempts to write to an offset of -1 relative to the allocated address. The practical impact of this vulnerability is that an attacker can utilize zero-length attribute entries to perform memory write operations, potentially leading to system crashes or remote code execution. The suggested fix is to reject zero-length attribute entries early in the validation process, as zero-length entries have no valid meaning within the XDomain attribute protocol. It is recommended to upgrade to a patched Linux kernel version.",
    tags_en: ["Linux Kernel", "Thunderbolt", "Buffer Overflow", "CVE-2026-53150", "drivers/thunderbolt/property.c"],
    sources: [
      { name: "NVD CVE API", url: "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-53150", lang: "EN" }
    ]
