    category: "Linux",
    title: "Linux 核心 nvmem 驅動程式修復 Use-After-Free 漏洞，避免錯誤路徑記憶體釋放後仍使用資源",
    summary: "本漏洞涉及 Linux 核心的 nvmem 驅動程式（位於 drivers/nvmem/core.c）。問題出在錯誤處理路徑（error paths）中，當呼叫 `__nvmem_device_put()` 釋放底層記憶體和資源後，程式碼仍繼續使用 `nvmem` 結構，導致 Use-After-Free (UAF) 漏洞。修復建議是確保在返回錯誤代碼之前，總是將 `nvmem` 設備的參考計數（reference）作為最後一步操作。NIST 提供了多個 Git 提交連結，指引開發者更新核心程式碼以修補此類錯誤。受影響的版本範圍較廣，建議所有使用相關核心模組的系統應立即更新至修復版本，以防止潛在的記憶體安全問題。",
    tags: ["Linux 核心", "nvmem", "Use-After-Free", "記憶體安全", "CVE-2026-53156"],
    title_en: "Linux Kernel nvmem Driver Fixes Use-After-Free Vulnerability, Preventing Resource Usage After Error Path Memory Release",
    summary_en: "This vulnerability affects the nvmem driver in the Linux kernel (located at drivers/nvmem/core.c). The issue resides in the error handling paths, where the code continues to use the `nvmem` structure even after calling `__nvmem_device_put()` to release underlying memory and resources, leading to a Use-After-Free (UAF) vulnerability. The suggested fix is to ensure that the `nvmem` device reference is decremented as the final step before returning an error code. NIST has provided multiple Git commit links, guiding developers to update the kernel code to patch this type of error. Since the affected version range is broad, all systems using the relevant kernel module are advised to update immediately to the patched version to prevent potential memory safety issues.",
    tags_en: ["Linux Kernel", "nvmem", "Use-After-Free", "Memory Safety", "CVE-2026-53156"],
    sources: [
      { name: "NVD CVE API", url: "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-53156", lang: "EN" }
    ]
