    title: "EU《網路韌性法案》（CRA）準備度持續落後：開源生態系統面臨供應鏈透明化壓力",
    summary: "最新的 2026 年《網路韌性法案》（EU CRA）準備度報告顯示，全球開源生態系統的意識與準備程度持續落後。報告指出，不了解該法規的受訪者比例已升至 66%，且此知識鴻溝甚至比前一年更廣。對於產品要在歐盟市場銷售的製造商而言，法規遵循的壓力日益增大，特別是 2026 年 9 月需開始報告積極利用的漏洞和嚴重安全事件。雖然部分組織開始產生軟體物料清單（SBOMs），但仍有大量企業依賴孤立的私有分支進行修補，這在 CRA 要求更高的透明度和可追溯性時，已成為不可持續的策略。此外，報告還揭示了開源專案的 CVE 數量激增（2026 年第一季年增 394%），凸顯了供應鏈安全風險的實質增加。建議企業應將上游貢獻視為核心的合規策略，而非可有可無的善意，以應對法規帶來的嚴格要求。",
    tags: ["EU CRA", "網路韌性法案", "SBOM", "開源安全", "供應鏈安全", "CVE"],
    title_en: "EU Cyber Resilience Act (CRA) Preparedness Lagging: Open Source Ecosystem Faces Supply Chain Transparency Pressure",
    summary_en: "The latest 2026 Cyber Resilience Act (EU CRA) preparedness report indicates that the global open source ecosystem's awareness and readiness are continuously lagging. The report points out that the proportion of respondents unaware of the regulation has risen to 66%, and this knowledge gap is even wider than in the previous year. For manufacturers whose products are to be sold in the EU market, the pressure for regulatory compliance is increasing, especially with the requirement to report actively exploited vulnerabilities and serious security incidents starting in September 2026. Although some organizations have begun generating Software Bill of Materials (SBOMs), many enterprises still rely on isolated private branches for patching, a strategy that is becoming unsustainable given the higher transparency and traceability required by the CRA. Furthermore, the report revealed a surge in the number of CVEs in open source projects (a 394% year-on-year increase in Q1 2026), highlighting a substantial increase in supply chain security risks. Companies are advised to treat upstream contributions as a core compliance strategy, rather than optional goodwill, to meet the strict requirements imposed by the regulation.",
