    summary_en: "According to a reliable leak source, Apple has decided to advance the development plan for the second-generation iPhone Ultra, which is expected to be released alongside the iPhone 18 Pro in September. While the source confirmed the foldable project for the Ultra 2, no new feature details were provided, and it is hinted that the screen might retain this year's design. However, Apple has not made a final decision regarding the production of the next-generation iPhone Air 3. The report suggests that Apple may be monitoring the market performance of the iPhone Air 2 (which is expected to feature an ultra-wide-angle lens) to assess whether to continue developing subsequent models. Overall, these product development plans are part of long-term planning, and market success remains the key determinant for whether they will be launched.",
