    summary_en: "Apple has released a new Siri App in iOS 27, featuring a chatbot interface that supports text, images, and file attachments. Although the App defaults to Siri AI, users can quickly switch to the ChatGPT chat model by long-pressing the input field and tapping \"Ask...\". Currently, users can choose between using Siri or ChatGPT as the chat provider within the Siri App. However, this feature has several limitations: the conversation context cannot be transferred when switching chat providers; furthermore, closing and reopening the App causes it to switch back to Siri, even if a ChatGPT conversation was in progress. There is currently no permanent setting to designate ChatGPT as the default model, though Apple may add support for other chatbots in the future. This update primarily enhances the flexibility for users to utilize multiple AI models within a single interface.",
