    title_en: "Apple Takes Over Swift Package Index, Plans to Remove Dependency on GitHub",
    summary_en: "Apple has announced its takeover of the Swift Package Index (SPM) and plans to remove its current dependency on GitHub. This move has significant implications for developers and the related ecosystem using the Swift language. SPM is the primary mechanism for managing and distributing Swift libraries across Apple platforms (such as iOS and macOS). The goal of removing the GitHub dependency may be to enhance supply chain security, ensure a more stable distribution source, or integrate it more closely into Apple's own ecosystem. For developers, this means that future dependency management processes will need adjustment, potentially requiring a shift toward using more controlled or Apple-recommended internal repositories. Although the article does not provide specific technical details or the scope of the impact, this represents a major adjustment by Apple regarding its development toolchain and ecosystem control. Developers should closely monitor official Apple migration guides and best practices.",
