    title_en: "Micron Executive Suggests Apple's Procurement Strategy Contributes to Memory Market Supply-Demand Imbalance",
    summary_en: "This article reports that Sumit Sadana, Chief Business Officer at Micron Technology, suggested during an interview with the Wall Street Journal that Apple's procurement strategies are impacting the current supply-demand imbalance in the memory market. Micron pointed out that during market troughs, some customers engage in overly aggressive low-price purchasing, preventing Micron from making necessary capital investments. Many industry investments stalled in 2023 due to excessively low prices and profit margins. While Apple's long-term procurement agreements allow it to lock in lower prices and avoid the shock of price increases, Micron believes this behavior also creates an unsustainable pricing environment, hindering investment in additional industry capacity. Apple had previously stated that due to memory supply shortages, it would raise product prices, but Micron argues that historically low market prices were the primary cause of insufficient industry investment.",
